# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Riccardo Farris et al. (2026). Bayesian neural networks versus deep ensembles for uncertainty quantification in machine learning interatomic potentials.
#   Machine Learning Science and Technology. doi:10.1088/2632-2153/ae9de8  arXiv:2509.19180v2
#
# Version read: arxiv-preprint arXiv:2509.19180v2 (sha256 e446633e9cb622bc...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 552 (Training/reliability). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
# Generated by artifacts/scripts/encode_paper.py from artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/farris2026.yaml.
#
# Encoding scope: aenet-PyTorch Behler-Parrinello networks (two hidden
# layers of 15 tanh units) trained as variational BNNs (LRT and RAD
# guides) or deep ensembles on the TiO2 dataset (high-data 6,330 and
# low-data 1,265 training structures) and on QM7 (energies only); test
# energy MAE/RMSE as averages over five runs (Tables 4 and 7). NLL and
# UQ calibration metrics are not schema metrics.

@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix schema: <https://schema.org/> .
@prefix mls: <http://www.w3.org/ns/mls#> .
@prefix unit: <http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/> .
@prefix mlips: <https://w3id.org/mlips#> .
@prefix entity: <https://w3id.org/mlips/entity/> .

###############################################################################
# Q1 -- Bibliographic identification
###############################################################################

entity:study-farris2026 a mlips:BenchmarkStudy ;
